  "result": "Perfect! All 247 tests pass (including 17 new lateFee tests). Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/reports.js`** now includes three reporting functions:\n\n1. **`overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)`** \u2014 Previously created\n   - Returns overdue invoices sorted by most overdue first\n\n2. **`vatSummary(invoices)`** \u2014 Previously created\n   - Returns VAT summary aggregated by rate, sorted descending\n\n3. **`lateFee(invoice, asOf)`** \u2014 Newly added function\n   - Calculates late fees at **0.04% per day**\n   - Returns `0` for:\n     - Draft invoices\n     - Paid invoices\n     - Invoices not yet due (dueDate \u2265 asOf)\n   - For overdue invoices:\n     - `lateFee = balanceDue(invoice) \u00d7 0.0004 \u00d7 daysOverdue`\n     - Properly rounded to whole cents\n   - Works with partially paid invoices (charges fee on remaining balance)\n\n**`test/reports.test.js`** \u2014 17 comprehensive lateFee tests covering:\n- Status checks (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Due date conditions (not due, on due date, overdue)\n- Fee calculations (1 day, multiple days, 30 days)\n- Partially paid invoices (fee on remaining balance)\n- Different payment terms (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Year boundary scenarios\n- Linear scaling with days (doubled days = doubled fee)\n- Multiple discount tiers\n- Edge cases (zero balance, small amounts, large amounts)\n\nAll 247 tests pass successfully (210 existing + 20 vatSummary + 17 lateFee).",
